The k24 skill-author found these in the UE LLM Toolkit source (github.com/ColtonWilley/ue-llm-toolkit; paths under Plugin/UELLMToolkit/Source/UELLMToolkit/Private/). The toolkit has no karr board, and an upstream issue is a public-tracker write, so reporting them is the maintainer's call. The shipped skills already steer agents around each one.
A (severe, possible editor crash): asset set_asset_property with a path ending in an array index (Tags.0) writes to the asset object's own address: MCP/Tools/MCPTool_Asset.cpp:1214-1218 with :1295.
B: MCP/MCPToolBase.cpp:80-105 handles byte properties before the enum branch at :176, so byte-enum names inside arrays are stored as 0 without an error.
C: MCP/Tools/MCPTool_SetProperty.cpp:162-167 silently skips an unmatched middle part of a property path.
D: MCP/Tools/MCPTool_Asset.cpp:1374 catches soft references before their own branches at :1393-1412; a soft path that does not load gives "Unsupported property type".
E: MCP/Tools/MCPTool_LevelQuery.cpp:98 drops the near-miss suggestions that info computes.
F: MCP/Tools/MCPTool_SpawnActor.cpp:64-67 passes name to the engine without checking whether it is taken.
Done when the maintainer has decided whether to report them upstream (and the skills are revised if upstream fixes land).

G (from the k24 review): asset_import batch_import with no .fbx files returns "Error: " with an empty message — the handler reads only the "message" field (MCP/Tools/MCPTool_AssetImport.cpp:152-166) while the error builder writes the text to "error" (AssetImporter.cpp:45-51, :281). The other import operations go through the helper at MCPTool_AssetImport.cpp:10-27 and report errors correctly.

