From k22/k23 (material, niagara, audio, metasound). Paths are under Source/UELLMToolkit/Private/ unless noted; the skills steer around each one.
Material (MCP/Tools/MCPTool_Material.cpp): M1 get_material_info never lists a material's exposed parameters: GetMaterialParameters (:705-752) is unused, instances return only their stored overrides (:667-695), and base materials return nothing (:697-700). M2 create only logs parameter failures as a warning and still saves (:230-234). M3 set_material_parameters keeps partial values on error, with no PostEditChange and no dirty mark (:298-306). M4 parameter names are not checked, and values of the wrong type are skipped silently (:585, :604, :630). M5 an omitted r, g or b leaves the default-constructed FLinearColor uninitialized (:606-611). M6 create does not check for an existing asset (:196-216). M7 MCPTool_Material.h:14 says Constant or Dynamic, but only Constant is created.
Niagara (MCP/Tools/MCPTool_Niagara.cpp): N1 spawn_system labels the owner of the SpawnSystemAtLocation component (:715-726), probably a shared actor such as World Settings, and persistence is unclear. N2 set_parameter reads vector and color components with GetNumberField and no defaults, alpha included (:615-657). N3 SetParameterData writes the asset's store without Modify or PostEditChange (:584-665). N4 value is declared string/number/object (:52), but no type accepts a string, and the bridge advertises it as a string.
Audio (AudioEditor.cpp, MCP/Tools/MCPTool_Audio.*): A1 set_audio_properties requires target_path (MCPTool_Audio.cpp:156), while the description says asset_path (MCPTool_Audio.h:48) and the schema lacks target_path. A2 is_spatialized writes bIsUISound = !value (AudioEditor.cpp:588), but the reader reports bAllowSpatialization (:336, :393). A3 set_audio_properties on a world actor never marks it or the level dirty (:508-562, :657-661). A4 inspect tests USoundWave before UMetaSoundSource (:61 vs :203), so the MetaSound branch is probably dead. A5 MCPTool_Audio.h:35 promises subtitle (and attenuation) for SoundWave; only attenuation_settings is returned. A6 create_sound_cue and create_attenuation neither save nor check for an existing asset, and the Sound Cue gets no editor graph (:683-702, :718-798). A7 'stubs' comments sit on implemented write operations (MCPTool_Audio.h:90, MCPTool_Audio.cpp:131, AudioEditor.cpp:411). A8 a failed sound or attenuation load in set_audio_properties leaves the earlier keys applied (:593-619). A9 unknown enum names are ignored silently; settings, db_attenuation_at_max, is_spatialized and spatialization_algorithm are undeclared, and a top-level shape is not copied, only attenuation_shape (MCPTool_Audio.cpp:241-281).
MetaSound (MetaSoundEditor.cpp, MCP/Tools/MCPTool_MetaSound.h): S1 create ignores output_format (:287-312). S2 add_node hard-codes major version 1 and passes no variant (:329-332). S3 connect ignores the AddEdge result (:421). S4 the descriptions disagree with the code: add_graph_input/add_graph_output return input_node_id/output_node_id (:596, :629), not node_id (h:68, :71); inspect's output_format (h:40) and get_graph's defaults (h:46) are not returned. S5 remove_node removes edges before the node (:366-371), so a failed removal still drops the edges. S6 preview reports status playing unconditionally (:664-669).
Bridge: B1 mcp-bridge/lib.js:118-147 maps integer (material_slot, max_results) and string/number/object to string.

